# .claude/ -- ignored by CONTENTS, not as a directory.
#
# `.claude/` on its own excludes the directory, and git then never descends into
# it, so a later `!.claude/hooks/` re-include is silently ignored. Excluding
# `.claude/*` instead leaves the directory walkable and makes the exceptions
# below actually take effect. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`.
.claude/*

# EXCEPT the design-lookup gate. An untracked gate protects only the machine it
# was written on: a runner box, a Codex worker, a fresh clone, or a worktree
# gets no enforcement at all -- which is exactly where an unresearched edit is
# most expensive and least visible. The gate and the settings that wire it up
# are repo policy, not machine config, so they ship with the repo.
# settings.local.json stays ignored: permissions and paths ARE machine-local.
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json

# Session report buffers are local-only, never committed (public repo)
_reports/

# Added by ggshield
.cache_ggshield

# qmd project-local search index (rebuildable; never commit)

# qmd project-local search index: the database is rebuildable
# and never committed; the allowlist config is tracked.
.qmd/*
!.qmd/index.yml
